2	4	AI Research	This note contains information about LangGraph architecture.	2026-09-30 07:17:52.535759	2026-09-30 07:17:52.535759
3	5	Persistence Test	This data must survive a Colab runtime reset.	2026-09-30 11:02:48.384922	2026-09-30 11:02:48.384922
5	1	Agent Test	Hello. This note was created by LangGraph.	2026-09-30 11:13:47.557927	2026-09-30 11:13:47.557927
6	4	Machine Learning	\nMachine learning is a field of artificial intelligence focused on learning\npatterns from data. Supervised learning uses labeled examples, while\nunsupervised learning discovers patterns without explicit labels. Model\nevaluation requires appropriate metrics, validation data, and careful control\nof overfitting.\n	2026-09-30 20:02:13.982193	2026-09-30 20:02:13.982193
7	4	PostgreSQL	\nPostgreSQL is a powerful open-source relational database system. It supports\ntransactions, foreign keys, indexing, full-text search, and extensible data\ntypes. The pgvector extension allows PostgreSQL to store and search vector\nembeddings for similarity-based retrieval.\n	2026-09-30 20:02:13.982193	2026-09-30 20:02:13.982193
8	4	LangGraph	\nLangGraph is a framework for building stateful applications and agentic\nworkflows with explicit graph structures. A graph can contain nodes,\nconditional routing, tools, and persistent state. LangGraph is useful when an\napplication needs controlled multi-step execution and reliable workflow\nmanagement.\n	2026-09-30 20:02:13.982193	2026-09-30 20:02:13.982193
9	4	Retrieval Augmented Generation	\nRetrieval augmented generation combines information retrieval with language\nmodel generation. A RAG system retrieves relevant documents or chunks before\ngenerating an answer. Hybrid retrieval can combine semantic search and\nkeyword search, followed by fusion and reranking to improve the relevance of\nthe final context.\n	2026-09-30 20:02:13.982193	2026-09-30 20:02:13.982193
10	4	Sports Science	\nSports performance depends on training, recovery, nutrition, and adaptation.\nStrength training can improve muscular strength and power, while aerobic\ntraining develops cardiovascular capacity. Training programs should consider\nprogressive overload, recovery periods, and individual performance goals.\n	2026-09-30 20:02:13.982193	2026-09-30 20:02:13.982193
\.


